th1-surjection-curation-001+math1-bijection-curation-001+math1-union-curation-001+math1-proper-curation-001+math1-complement-curation-001+math1-complement-render-001+math1-division-curation-001+math1-reciprocal-curation-001+math1-inequality-curation-001+math1-inequality-feedback-001+math1-maximum-curation-001+math1-minimum-curation-001+math1-boundedset-curation-001+math1-endpoint-curation-001+audit-groups-20261027+topup-math-i-20261028+topup-math-ii-20261028+topup-pt-20261028+topup-math-iii-20261028","history_only":true,"curation_sha256":"402117cd2ecc28eaf6387aaefcadec5f0c0540f0912f8a96983845daf37ec8e2","concept_id":"Year-1/1a-OR-Modelling/nonconvex-region-modelling.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/1a-OR-Modelling/nonconvex-region-modelling.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_nonconvex_region_modelling_921ae5a8_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For the region of points $(x_1,x_2)$ with $x_1,x_2\\ge0$, $x_1+x_2\\le3$, and either $x_2\\le1$ or $x_2\\ge2$, modelled with binary $y$ and the switch $x_2\\le1+My$, $x_2\\ge2-M(1-y)$ with a valid $M$, while $x_1+x_2\\le3$ and $x_1,x_2\\ge0$ stay unswitched, which piece does the value $y=1$ select?","options":["The upper piece, where $x_2\\ge2$ is enforced","The lower piece, where $x_2\\le1$ is enforced","Both pieces at once, so no point fits","Neither piece, so the gap is allowed"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0b1b49263899c78611f8e6e6","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_nonconvex_region_modelling_921ae5a8_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Either-or constraints express an inclusive 'or': both inequalities may hold. Why is this harmless for the region of points $(x_1,x_2)$ with $x_1,x_2\\ge0$, $x_1+x_2\\le3$, and either $x_2\\le1$ or $x_2\\ge2$?","options":["It is not harmless: inclusive 'or' admits the gap $1<x_2<2$.","It is harmless because the binary $y$ cannot take both values.","It is harmless because inclusive 'or' enforces both inequalities.","It is harmless as no point meets $x_2\\le1$ and $x_2\\ge2$ at once."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4ae91921296f19a4b07d8543","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_nonconvex_region_modelling_921ae5a8_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Consider the region of points $(x_1,x_2)$ with $x_1,x_2\\ge0$, $x_1+x_2\\le3$, and either $x_2\\le1$ or $x_2\\ge2$, with the extra constraint $x_1\\ge1.5$. What is the largest value of $x_2$ in this region?","options":["1","1.5","2","3"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bb9b7b0e597716efaf44769b","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"}]}}